xceeds about 5/7, roughly 0.71. Since both copies share the same model and essay, I'd put that correlation high, with the differing observations only changing names and leads, so I'll choose to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether A-FDT with a twin copy still applies when the two copies see different observations, given the payoffs for quiet and send. I'm asking whether the other copy's action depends on my decision procedure, using the essay's test of whether it computes, copies, or models my reasoning, and noting that it's the same model with similar reasoning.\n\nI'm working out the cooperation threshold: cooperating pays off once the chance the other copy mirrors me exceeds about 5/7, roughly 0.71. Since both copies share the same model and essay, I'd put that correlation high, with the differing observations only changing names and leads, so I'll choose to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10306,"completion_tokens":1044,"total_tokens":11350,"cost":0.031052,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.031052,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020612,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01044},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":638,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}